# The landing site is a whole folder, not a handful of files. Listing them one
# by one kept leaking the rest into commits: the copy of the site brought its
# own CNAME, blackhole.js, killswitch-motion.*, app-mock.css and flag assets,
# none of which the explicit list above covered.
public/CNAME
public/blackhole.js
public/killswitch-motion.css
public/killswitch-motion.js
public/app-mock.css
public/screen-games.jpg
public/screen-servers.jpg
public/screen-*-material.jpg
# The landing site keeps its own handful of flag svgs at the root, separate
# from the app's full set under public/flags/.
public/de.svg
public/fi.svg
public/nl.svg
public/pl.svg
public/us.svg
public/flags/dd.dd
# The zipped site update, built to hand over to the marketing repo.
wawity-site-update.zip
# Promo films and their Remotion sources. 31MB of mp4 that the client never
# loads; they belong to the marketing repo. The two zips alongside them are
# build output that duplicates what is already in those folders.
public/promo/
public/_promo-src/
public/promo-player.css
public/promo-player.js
public/wawity-site-demos.zip
wawity-fix.zip

# Session tooling (not part of the project)
.opencode/
temp-skills/
